However, given that `boost::json` does in fact provide full streaming capability to/from its DOM, it becomes very attractive to allow the network layer to simply parse/serialize to/from the json DOM for both the `json-rpc` request/response classes, and the contained `request::params`/`response::result` objects. These objects we defined as (tiny bit simplified):
